    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "id": "gauge_pressure_calculator",
      "content": "## Gauge Pressure Calculator\n\nGauge pressure is the pressure difference between a system and atmospheric pressure: pg = ps - patm",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "system_pressure",
          "label": "System Pressure",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "Pa",
          "defaultValue": 150000
        },
        {
          "id": "atmospheric_pressure",
          "label": "Atmospheric Pressure",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "Pa",
          "defaultValue": 101325
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "gauge_pressure",
          "label": "Gauge Pressure",
          "unit": "Pa",
          "format": "decimal",
          "formula": "inputs.system_pressure - inputs.atmospheric_pressure"
        },
        {
          "id": "gauge_pressure_bar",
          "label": "Gauge Pressure",
          "unit": "bar",
          "format": "decimal",
          "formula": "(inputs.system_pressure - inputs.atmospheric_pressure) / 100000"
        },
        {
          "id": "gauge_pressure_psi",
          "label": "Gauge Pressure",
          "unit": "psi",
          "format": "decimal",
          "formula": "(inputs.system_pressure - inputs.atmospheric_pressure) / 6894.76"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "pressure_info",
      "content": "## Pressure Definitions\n\n### Absolute Pressure\n**Absolute pressure** (pabs) is measured relative to absolute zero pressure (the pressure at absolute vacuum). All calculations involving gas laws require pressure to be in absolute units.\n\n### Gauge Pressure\n**Gauge pressure** (pg) is the pressure difference between a system and the surrounding atmosphere, often measured with a gauge: pg = ps - patm\n\n### Standard Atmospheric Pressure\nThe **Standard Atmospheric Pressure** at sea-level (273 K / 0°C) is:\n- **1.01325 bar**\n- **101,325 Pa (absolute)**\n- **14.696 psi**\n- **760 mmHg**\n- **10.33 mH₂O**\n- **29.92 inHg**\n\n### Standard Pressure Conversion\n- 1 bar = 100,000 Pa = 0.9869 atm = 14.5 psi\n- 1 atmosphere = 101,325 Pa = 760 torr = 14.696 psi = 1.013 bar\n- 1 millibar = 100 Pa = 0.001 bar = 0.750 torr\n"
    }
  ]
